@startuml hld-04_engine_track
title HLD-04 — Engine track: what lives where, and when it moves (§8)\nBuild in the app with an Engine-shaped layout; lift to the Engine when the lift criterion is met
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction

package "Engine today (2.4.0)" #WhiteSmoke {
  [IExtension · ExtensionDescriptor\nExtensionManager] as E1
  [IContainer · IEventBus\nQtEventBridge · IDispatcher] as E2
  [Scheduler · HostedServiceManager] as E3
  [pyside_mvc: PresenterManager\ncreate_quick_widget · tokens · kit] as E4
}

package "App Phase 0–1: built in core/ and shell/ with NO app import (lift-ready)" #LightYellow {
  [core/contracts/BoundedContextModule\n(IExtension + contribute + subscribe)] as A1
  [core/contracts/contribution\nIContributionRegistry · Place · SizeHint\nContributionDescriptor] as A2
  [shell/workbench\nSurface = PageShell + place slots\nrender contributions per place] as A3
  [shell/navigation\nrestore vs user intent · can_leave] as A4
}

package "Engine later (EPIC-001D / TASK-043) — lifted when criterion met" #LightGreen {
  [extensions/workbench\nWorkbenchModule base · ContributionRegistry\nPlace vocabulary · Surface runtime] as L1
  [extensions/workbench/NavigationService\nUSER_INTENT vs RESTORE · can_leave] as L2
  [create_quick_widget(import_paths=)] as L3
  [ScheduledJob.cancel()] as L4
  [screen conformance suite] as L5
}

package "Stays in the app forever (policy)" #LightGray {
  [module list · which surfaces exist\ncontribution kinds such as dev_probe\ndev.mode gate · Binance gateway] as P1
}

A1 --> E1 : extends
A2 ..> E2 : registered in DI
A3 ..> E4 : PageShell, QuickSurface
A4 ..> E4 : PresenterManager
A1 ..> L1 : lift (Phase 2)
A2 ..> L1 : lift (Phase 2)
A3 ..> L1 : lift (Phase 5)
A4 ..> L2 : lift (Phase 5)
E3 ..> L4 : add now (small)
E4 ..> L3 : add when ADR D6 reopens
P1 ..> L1 : consumes

note bottom of A1
  Lift criterion (all three):
  1. zero imports from modules/, support/, shell/ (guard)
  2. used by >= 2 surfaces or >= 2 modules in this app
  3. the API has been stable for one full phase
end note
@enduml
